{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#142","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#142","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#142\",\"parent_revision\":\"def08d0d45ec4e26ea261878b73fb4fea642b5f0bea6a36354f503554be5f151\",\"root_revision\":\"def08d0d45ec4e26ea261878b73fb4fea642b5f0bea6a36354f503554be5f151\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`scripts/post_coverage_summary.test.mjs` defines 3 test cases. Nothing executes them.\\n\\n```\\n$ grep -rn \\\"node --test\\\" .github/ .pre-commit-config.yaml\\n$\\n```\\n\\nPR #104 advertised the tests when it moved the coverage-summary logic out of the workflow. The move was correct and #42 is closed on it \u2014 but the tests that came with it are dead weight until something runs them.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Why It Matters Here Specifically\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe whole point of the \\\"no inline CI code\\\" rule is that logic in `scripts/` can be linted and unit-tested. `.mjs` is linted (oxlint/oxfmt, `.pre-commit-config.yaml:78-90`). It is not tested. Half the rule's benefit is unrealised.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun `node --test scripts/` from CI, or from a prek hook. Note #127 \u2014 prek pins its own node toolchain, so a `language: node` hook will not run locally on macOS 12; a CI step avoids that.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #42 \u2014 where the script landed\\n- #104 \u2014 the PR\\n- #127 \u2014 prek's pinned node toolchain\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3a73d4b120f269c922a58479ff4ed37c1d4d2029ead8bfa473bff59e81e7ba27\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-08w\"}"}